WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:04.469
The next tool I'd like to talk about in optimization tools

2
00:00:04.469 --> 00:00:08.009
is how to bulk edit number of assets.

3
00:00:08.009 --> 00:00:09.990
Now let's say, for example, you want

4
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.929
to adjust all of the texture compression settings,

5
00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:14.169
or maybe some of your textures

6
00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:16.489
are not put into the correct texture group.

7
00:00:16.489 --> 00:00:18.649
While you could open up each one individually

8
00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:20.690
and apply this information, this

9
00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.609
can be tedious, especially if you have

10
00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:25.370
hundreds of textures to adjust.

11
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.570
The Bulk Edit option allows you

12
00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.129
to select many textures inside of the Content Browser.

13
00:00:31.129 --> 00:00:33.770
Then we can right-click on them, go to Asset Actions,

14
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.450
and select the Edit Selection and Property Matrix.

15
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.490
This will then open up those textures inside

16
00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.570
of the Property Matrix, which looks like the following image.

17
00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:48.329
And then from there, we can adjust their properties

18
00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:51.530
on the right-hand side of the Pinch column.

19
00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.130
And it will adjust the properties

20
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.530
that we have for our textures.

21
00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.090
Let's go ahead and take a look at how we do this in the editor.

22
00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.250
So we're going to come here and hit Control-Space.

23
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.549
I'm going to make sure my Content folder is selected.

24
00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:04.090
I'm going to grab just Textures.

25
00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.650
And for now, I'm going to hit Underscore In because I

26
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.730
know that there's a number of normal maps here.

27
00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.650
So I'm just going to select these first five,

28
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:14.879
right-click, and then Asset Actions, Edit Selection

29
00:01:14.879 --> 00:01:16.120
and Property Matrix.

30
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.519
Now that I've done that, you're

31
00:01:17.519 --> 00:01:19.519
going to see that it does come up.

32
00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:21.719
And let's come over here and adjust something

33
00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:22.879
like the LOD Bias.

34
00:01:22.879 --> 00:01:25.239
I'm just going to set this to a value of 1.

35
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.400
And if we hit this pin here, we'll

36
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.079
see that the LOD Bias has been, in fact, set to 1.

37
00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:34.000
And we can further check this by hovering

38
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.359
over each one of the textures.

39
00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:40.230
You can see the LOD Bias has been set to 1.

40
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.109
And just as easily to remove that,

41
00:01:42.109 --> 00:01:44.069
if we just set this to 0 again, we're

42
00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:45.989
going to set everything in here back to 0.

43
00:01:45.989 --> 00:01:48.510
So you can see how easy that is, especially

44
00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:51.150
if you have hundreds of assets that you wish to do.

45
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.670
Now, the last thing that I want to note about this tool,

46
00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.170
and I said this in the beginning,

47
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.670
but this is very important.

48
00:01:56.709 --> 00:01:59.629
This only works on things of the same asset type.

49
00:01:59.629 --> 00:02:02.469
So if I want to work on static meshes,

50
00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:04.750
I need to make sure I have static meshes selected.

51
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.909
If I want to work on skeletal meshes,

52
00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:09.110
I need to make sure I only have skeletal meshes.

53
00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.389
Same with textures.

54
00:02:11.389 --> 00:02:14.469
Making sure that you only have the right asset selected

55
00:02:14.469 --> 00:02:16.550
will ensure that all the properties are displayed

56
00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:20.669
and the tool works exactly how you need it to.
